.TH CLAUTOLISP 1 "October 2026" "clautolisp 2.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clautolisp \- standalone AutoLISP evaluator and interactive REPL.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clautolisp
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ FILE.lsp ]
.br
.B clautolisp
.RI [ options ]
.B \-l
.I FILE.lsp
.br
.B clautolisp
.RI [ options ]
.B \-x
.I EXPRESSION
.br
.B clautolisp
.RI [ options ]
.RB { \-l
.IR FILE " | " \-x " " EXPR }
.B \-i
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clautolisp
is a Common Lisp implementation of the AutoLISP / Visual LISP
runtime. It reads AutoLISP source files (or
.B \-x
expressions, or stdin via the interactive REPL), evaluates each
form in a fresh runtime session under a chosen dialect, and exits
with a meaningful status code. With no
.B \-l
/
.B \-x
/ positional argument and no
.BR \-i ,
the REPL is the implicit default.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Input selection
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-load " " \fIFILE\fR
Load and evaluate FILE. Equivalent to the positional form.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-eval " " \fIEXPR\fR
Evaluate EXPR instead of reading a file.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Enter the REPL after the action queue is drained (same context).
.SS Dialect
.TP
.BR \-\-dialect " " \fINAME\fR
One of:
.BR strict " (default), " autocad-2026 ", " bricscad-v26 .
.TP
.BR \-\-strict ", " \-\-autocad ", " \-\-bricscad ", " \-\-clautolisp
Shorthands for the matching
.BR \-\-dialect .
.TP
.B \-\-lax
Shorthand for
.BR "\-\-dialect lax" :
every extension available, no out-of-dialect diagnostic.
.SS Host (HAL backend)
.TP
.BR \-\-host " " \fIBACKEND\fR
.BR cador " (default), " cadtui ", or " nihil .
.B cador
is the headless in-process CAD core;
.B cadtui
is the full textual UI-tree host on that core (menus, drawings, CAD view,
DCL dialogs mirrored into an inspectable tree \(em cador is its degenerate
.I /application/console
configuration);
.B nihil
is the trivial backend.
.B mock
is a deprecated alias of cador;
.BR null " / " none
are deprecated aliases of nihil. See
.BR \-\-list-hosts .
.TP
.BR \-\-dwg " " \fIFILE\fR
Start on the drawing FILE (DXF or DWG): the first open drawing, current, in
place of the untitled Drawing1.dwg.
.TP
.BR \-\-mock-input " " \fIPATH\fR
Feed the file at PATH to the MockHost as its prompt-stream.
.TP
.BR \-\-gui " " \fICMD\fR
Subprocess command speaking the DCL sexp wire protocol.
.TP
.BR \-\-dcl " " \fI{tui,gui,auto}\fR
DCL renderer selection.
.B tui
forces the terminal form,
.B gui
uses the
.B \-\-gui
subprocess driver, and
.B auto
(the default) picks the GUI when a driver is configured and stdout is a
TTY, so every headless or piped run gets the terminal form.
.TP
.B \-\-trace
Print every AutoLISP call (entry args + exit value) on stderr.
.TP
.BR \-\-front-end-bindings " " \fIFILE\fR
Install the
.B *AUTOLISP\-...*
values a driving front end resolved (FILE, written by it) instead of
deriving them from this command line.
.B "alfe \-\-clautolisp \-\-backend subprocess"
passes it, so a program sees the same values as under alfe's in-process
engine.
.TP
.BR \-\-front-end-action-boundaries " " \fIDIR\fR
Stop before and after each action (each
.BR \-l ,
.BR \-x ,
and the REPL) and wait for the driving front end, which talks to the
program through files in DIR.
.B "alfe \-\-clautolisp \-\-backend subprocess"
passes it when a plug-in has per-action hooks, so the hooks run between
two actions of one run, as under alfe's in-process engine.
.SS Debugger (aldo)
.TP
.BR \-\-on-error " " \fIPOLICY\fR
What an uncaught AutoLISP error does:
.BR quit " (report and exit — the batch default), " debug
(break into the aldo debugger — the interactive-REPL default), or
.BR ignore .
Sets
.BR *CLAL-ON-ERROR* .
.TP
.BR \-\-on-interrupt " " \fIPOLICY\fR
What Control-C (SIGINT) does:
.BR debug " (break into the debugger at the interrupt point — the default),"
.BR ignore " (execution resumes), or " quit " (exit 130)."
Sets
.BR *CLAL-ON-INTERRUPT* ,
re-read live at each interrupt. A second Control-C while one is being
handled exits immediately. Applies to the SBCL and the CCL builds alike
(not to the Windows SBCL build, which keeps the console behaviour).
.BR alfe (1)
accepts the same debugger options for its
.B \-\-clautolisp
backend.
.TP
.BR \-\-on-quit " " \fIPOLICY\fR
What
.BR (quit) " / " (exit)
does:
.BR quit " (default) or " debug
(break into the debugger before the stack unwinds; continue quits,
abort cancels). Sets
.BR *CLAL-ON-QUIT* ,
re-read live at each call.
.TP
.BR \-\-debugger-ui " " \fIUI\fR
Debugger front-end:
.BR tui ", " ncurses ", or " aldb
(Emacs). Per-run override of the persisted
.B default-user-interface
aldo setting (default tui).
.TP
.BR \-\-aldb-listen " " \fR[\fIHOST\fR:]\fIPORT\fR
Bind the aldb (Emacs) listener; HOST defaults to 127.0.0.1, PORT 0
picks a free port. Implies
.BR "\-\-debugger-ui aldb" .
.TP
.B \-\-aldb-stdio
Use stdin/stdout as the aldb RPC channel; implies
.BR "\-\-debugger-ui aldb" ;
mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-interactive " and " \-\-aldb-listen .
.SS REPL and diagnostics
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the REPL banner.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print extra diagnostic information.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Debug traces, including CL backtraces on runtime errors.
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable ANSI colour in AutoLISP value output. Honoured equivalently
via
.BR $NO_COLOR " (" https://no-color.org ).
.SS Source-file encoding
.TP
.BR \-e " " \fIENC\fR
Override the default source-file encoding for this session.
Encoding names are case-insensitive. Mandatory:
.BR UTF-8 ", " ISO-8859-1 ", " WINDOWS-1252 ", " US-ASCII .
Run
.B clautolisp \-\-list-encodings
for the full catalogue, including the
.BR \-mac " / " \-dos " / " \-unix " / " \-lf " / " \-cr " / " \-crlf
line-terminator suffixes.
.TP
.BR \-E " " \fIENC\fR
Declared terminal-IO encoding. Surfaced as
.B *AUTOLISP-TERMINAL-ENCODING*
to user code. The CL streams are not rebound at runtime — terminal
IO is line-buffered.
.SS Init files
.TP
.BR \-norc ", " \-\-no-init
Skip user init files
.RB ( ~/.clautolisp{,rc} ", " ~/.autolisp{,rc} ", "
.IR ~/.config/clautolisp/init ", "
.IR ~/.config/autolisp/init ).
Honoured equivalently via
.BR $AUTOLISP_NO_INIT " / " $CLAUTOLISP_NO_INIT .
.SS Informational
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the
.B \-\-help
banner and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list-encodings
Print every encoding name accepted by
.BR \-e " / " \-E
(mandatory four + every encoding the running CL implementation
exposes) and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list-dialects
Print every
.B \-\-dialect
name, strict first and lax last, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list-hosts
Print the
.B \-\-host
backends, one per line with a short summary, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list-situations
Print the encoding situations settable with
.BR \-E\fIsituation\fR [ \-\fIdir\fR ]
and their defaults, then exit. Under a backend flag, show that
backend's defaults and where each comes from.
.SH "*AUTOLISP-…* GLOBALS"
clautolisp publishes a set of
.B *AUTOLISP-…*
globals in the running AutoLISP image, reflecting the CLI options
that launched it
.RB ( *AUTOLISP-BACKEND* ", " *AUTOLISP-DIALECT* ", "
.BR *AUTOLISP-VERSION* ", " *AUTOLISP-FILE-ENCODING* ", " *AUTOLISP-ACTIONS* ", "
…). See the user-manual for the full table.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LC_ALL\fR, \fBLANG\fR, \fBLC_CTYPE
Probed in that order for the default source-file and terminal
encoding when
.B \-e
/
.B \-E
are not given.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable ANSI colour output (https://no-color.org).
.TP
.B AUTOLISP_NO_INIT\fR, \fBCLAUTOLISP_NO_INIT
Equivalent to
.BR \-norc .
.TP
.B CLAUTOLISP_GUI
DCL GUI driver command, used when
.B \-\-gui
is omitted.
.TP
.B CLAUTOLISP_DCL_DEBUG
When set and non-empty, trace the DCL subprocess renderer on standard
error, each line prefixed
.BR [dcl-debug] .
.TP
.B CLAUTOLISP_BACKGROUND
.BR dark " or " light :
override the detected terminal background.
.B COLORFGBG
and
.B TMUX
are consulted next when it is unset.
.TP
.B CLAUTOLISP_DWG_LIBDIR
Directory holding the DWG codec shared library, searched before the
development tree and the installed layout.
.TP
.B CLAUTOLISP_PREFIX
.B $PREFIX
used to build the trusted search path; omitted when unset.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR, \fBXDG_CONFIG_DIRS
Where
.IR lisp.conf " and " aldo.conf
are read and written.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Contributes
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/autolisp/
to the trusted search path.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Where the default dribble log is written.
.TP
.B CLAUTOLISP_DEBUG_PATHMAP
When set to any value, dump the recorded build frame and the detected
run frame of the path-mapping layer to standard error at startup.
Diagnostic aid on Windows, where MSYS2, Cygwin, WSL and native
programs spell the same file differently; a no-op elsewhere, where the
mapping is the identity.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.clautolisp\fR, \fB~/.clautolisprc\fR, \fB~/.autolisp\fR, \fB~/.autolisprc
User init files, loaded before any
.BR \-l " / " \-x .
.TP
.B ~/.config/clautolisp/init\fR, \fB~/.config/autolisp/init
XDG variant of the init files.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Apart from 1 and 130, the codes of
.BR sysexits.h ,
with the same values on every system, MS-Windows included:
.TP
.BR 0 " (EX_OK)"
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The AutoLISP program failed: a runtime error escaped it.
.TP
.BR 64 " (EX_USAGE)"
Command-line usage error: unknown option, missing argument, invalid
value;
.B \-\-dwg
on a host without drawings.
.TP
.BR 65 " (EX_DATAERR)"
A
.B \-l
file or
.B \-x
expression the reader refuses (unbalanced parenthesis, bytes not valid
in the source encoding); a
.B \-\-dwg
file that is not a drawing.
.TP
.BR 66 " (EX_NOINPUT)"
An input file does not exist or is not readable: the
.B \-l
file, the
.B \-\-dwg
drawing, the
.B \-\-mock\-input
file.
.TP
.BR 69 " (EX_UNAVAILABLE)"
The DWG native library a
.B \-\-dwg
drawing needs is absent.
.TP
.BR 70 " (EX_SOFTWARE)"
Internal error.
.TP
.BR 73 " (EX_CANTCREAT)"
The
.B \-\-dribble
transcript cannot be created.
.TP
.BR 74 " (EX_IOERR)"
Input/output error.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted (Control-C under the
.B quit
interrupt policy; 128 + SIGINT).
.PP
Before clautolisp 2.2.215 a file that could not be opened exited 2 and
every other failure 1; a script testing for 2 must test for 66.
.PP
These are the codes
.B clautolisp
itself produces. An AutoLISP program may choose its own status with the
clautolisp extensions
.BR "(autolisp-set-status " N ")"
and
.BR "(quit " [ N ])
\(em
.B (quit)
with no argument exits with the status recorded earlier, 0 by default.
A caller cannot distinguish such a status from the ones above.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR alfe (1),
.BR read-autolisp (1).
.PP
Full documentation as info pages:
.B info clautolisp-user-manual
or
.B info clautolisp-specifications .
